tiplexing, Circuit Switching, Packet Switching, ATM and Frame Relay.',1,NULL,3,NULL,'2025-03-17 11:00:09','2025-03-17 11:00:09'),(794,'Data communications','William L. Schweber','McGraw-Hill',2000,NULL,500,'English','','Data communications covers the fast-moving dynamic field of communications. This area of study involves the sending and receiving of information in digital format over                                                  distances ranging from a few inches to thousands of miles. Topics cover in this book are:\no	An introduction to communications\no	Communications channel characteristics\no	Modulation\no	Analog communications and multiplexing\no	Digital communications\no	Communications, media, and problems\no	Communications system requirements\no	The RS-232 interface standard\no	Other communications interfaces\no	Telephone system and modems\no	Networks\no	Error detection, correction, and data security\no	Test techniques and instrumentation\n',1,NULL,3,NULL,'2025-03-17 11:00:09','2025-03-17 11:00:09'),(795,'Data communications: beyond the basic','','McGraw-Hill',2000,NULL,500,'English','','The topics from this book are:\n1. planning & design\n2. Technology\n3. Application\n4. Management\n5. Futures\n',1,NULL,3,NULL,'2025-03-17 11:00:09','2025-03-17 11:00:09'),(796,'Data Mining: a Tutorial Based Primer','Richard J. Roiger','Pearson education',2000,NULL,500,'','','Topics covers in this book are;\n1. Data mining fundamentals.\n2. Tools for knowledge discovery.\n3. Advanced data mining techniques.\n4. Intelligent systems',1,NULL,3,NULL,'2025-03-17 11:00:09','2025-03-17 11:00:09'),(797,'Data processing in public and university libr','John Haervey edited','Spartan Books',2000,NULL,500,'English','','',1,NULL,3,NULL,'2025-03-17 11:00:09','2025-03-17 11:00:09'),(798,'Data structures using C and C++','Yedidyah Langsam et.al','Prentice Hall of India',2000,NULL,500,'English','','Features of this book :\n1. Algorithms are explained in detail and analyzed showing step by step solutions to real world problems\n2. Issues and pitfalls that may occur as algorithms are transformed in to programs are discussed \n3. Each data structure is implemented in a variety of ways that demonstrate the real choices and trade-offs programmers face.\n4. Working program in  C and C++ are used to teach the reader how to produce readable basic data structures such as stacks, linked list, and trees.\n5. Concept are illustrated by excellent examples \n6. Diagram are used extensively throughout the text\n7. Over 400 exercises are included that vary widely in type and difficulty, involving the reader in modification of programs and algorithms.\n\n',1,NULL,9,NULL,'2025-03-17 11:00:09','2025-03-17 11:00:09'),(799,'Data structures using C and C++: 2nd edition','Yedidayah Langsam dkk','Prentice Hall of India',2000,NULL,500,'English','','',1,NULL,3,NULL,'2025-03-17 11:00:09','2025-03-17 11:00:09'),(800,'Data Structures with C++ : Shaum\'s outline of','John R. Hubbard','McGraw Hill',2000,NULL,500,'English','','Inside this book, you\'ll find:\n1. Full coverage of Computer Science I-II, using the computing language taught by 83% of all colleges.\n2. Simplified explanations of recursion, logic, polymorphism, algorithms, and more.\n3. 455 solved problems in computer science, including step-by-step annotations.\n4. Examples and worked problems that help you master data structures with C++.',1,NULL,9,NULL,'2025-03-17 11:00:09','2025-03-17 11:00:09'),(801,'Database Acces with Visual Basic 6','Jeffrey P. McManus','Sams',2000,NULL,500,'English','','',1,NULL,3,NULL,'2025-03-17 11:00:09','2025-03-17 11:00:09'),(802,'Database access with Visual Basic 6','Jeffrey P. McManus','Sams',2000,NULL,500,'English','','Learn the concepts, design databases, build user interfaces, and write queries. Build the applications create three tier cliet server system based on the following technologies:\n1. Data Access objects\n2. Remote data objects\n3. Activex data Ojects 2.0\n4. The component