,500,'English','','There are ten topics included in this book, that is: Privacy Under Attack, Database Nation, Absolute Identification, What did you do today?, The view from Above, To Know Your Future, Buy Now!, Who Owns Your Information?, Kooks and Terrorists, Excuse me, But Are You Human?',1,NULL,3,NULL,'2025-03-17 11:00:09','2025-03-17 11:00:09'),(808,'Database nation: the death of privacy in the ','Simson Garfinkel','O\'Reilly',2000,NULL,500,'English','','The contens book is:\n1.privacy under Atack\n2.Database nation \n3.Absolute idenfication\n4.What did you do today?\n5.the view from above',1,NULL,3,NULL,'2025-03-17 11:00:09','2025-03-17 11:00:09'),(809,'Database Programming with JDBC and Java','George Reese','O\'Reilly And Shroff Publ.',2000,NULL,500,'English','','The book begins with a quick overview of SQL for developers who may be asked to handle a database for the first time. It then explains how to issue database queries and updates through SQL and JDBC. It also covers the use of stored procedures and other measures to improve efficiency, where these are available.',1,NULL,6,NULL,'2025-03-17 11:00:09','2025-03-17 11:00:09'),(810,'Database programming with Visual Basic 6 in 2','Curtis Smith','Techmedia',2000,NULL,500,'English','','Topics cover in this book are:\n1. Discover the new database features and components of Visual Basic 6.\n2. Use Active Data Objects to connect to a data source.\n3. Use design features such as database normalization, replication, and security.\n4. Create and update databases with Visual Basic 6 using SQL.\n5. Program an ODBC interface to remote databases.\n6. Implement data-bound controls.\n7. Access network-based databases using remote Data Objects.\n8. Generate reports using the Data Report Designer.\n9. Create programs with the Data environtment designer.',1,NULL,3,NULL,'2025-03-17 11:00:09','2025-03-17 11:00:09'),(811,'Database publishing with filemaker pro on the','Maria Langer','Peachpit Press',2000,NULL,500,'English','',''